0000 - cctns,32,"Using colour: Colour should be used with care, taking into account human capabilities and restrictions in perceiving colour, and not as the only means of conveying information. Color should never be the only means of coding. Some users may have difficulties in perceiving certain colors or color combinations (color-blindness).","[{""claim_id"": ""32-C1"", ""claim"": ""Using colour: Colour should be used with care, taking into account human capabilities and restrictions in perceiving colour, and not as the only means of conveying information."", ""claim_text"": ""Using colour: Colour should be used with care, taking into account human capabilities and restrictions in perceiving colour, and not as the only means of conveying information."", ""claim_kind"": ""OBSERVABLE_CORE"", ""claim_type"": ""OBSERVABLE"", ""importance"": ""CORE"", ""status"": ""MISSING"", ""source"": ""requirement_decomposition""}, {""claim_id"": ""32-C2"", ""claim"": ""Color should never be the only means of coding."", ""claim_text"": ""Color should never be the only means of coding."", ""claim_kind"": ""OBSERVABLE_CORE"", ""claim_type"": ""OBSERVABLE"", ""importance"": ""CORE"", ""status"": ""MISSING"", ""source"": ""requirement_decomposition""}, {""claim_id"": ""32-C3"", ""claim"": ""Some users may have difficulties in perceiving certain colors or color combinations (color-blindness)."", ""claim_text"": ""Some users may have difficulties in perceiving certain colors or color combinations (color-blindness)."", ""claim_kind"": ""OBSERVABLE_CORE"", ""claim_type"": ""OBSERVABLE"", ""importance"": ""CORE"", ""status"": ""MISSING"", ""source"": ""requirement_decomposition""}]",NFR,PARTIALLY_UI_VERIFIABLE,NONE,TEXT_OR_ELEMENT_PRESENCE,MEDIUM,"Visible UI elements can show whether non-color cues are also present, but accessibility adequacy is broader."
0000 - cctns,33,"Using frames with care: If frames are used, care should be taken to avoid possible problems, for example, those involving the use of the back button, bookmarking of pages, or scrolling of information. When frames are used, it is important to title each frame, and to describe its purpose and how frames relate to one another other.","[{""claim_id"": ""33-C1"", ""claim"": ""If frames are used, care should be taken to avoid possible problems, for example, those involving the use of the back button, bookmarking of pages, or scrolling of information."", ""claim_text"": ""If frames are used, care should be taken to avoid possible problems, for example, those involving the use of the back button, bookmarking of pages, or scrolling of information."", ""claim_kind"": ""OBSERVABLE_CORE"", ""claim_type"": ""OBSERVABLE"", ""importance"": ""CORE"", ""status"": ""MISSING"", ""source"": ""requirement_decomposition""}, {""claim_id"": ""33-C2"", ""claim"": ""When frames are used, it is important to title each frame, and to describe its purpose and how frames relate to one another other."", ""claim_text"": ""When frames are used, it is important to title each frame, and to describe its purpose and how frames relate to one another other."", ""claim_kind"": ""OBSERVABLE_CORE"", ""claim_type"": ""OBSERVABLE"", ""importance"": ""CORE"", ""status"": ""MISSING"", ""source"": ""requirement_decomposition""}]",NFR,PARTIALLY_UI_VERIFIABLE,NONE,TEXT_OR_ELEMENT_PRESENCE,LOW,"Frame titles and descriptions may be visible, but back-button or bookmarking behavior is not fully judgeable from screenshots."
0000 - cctns,34,"Providing alternatives to frame-based presentation: If frames are used, an alternative way of presenting relevant information without frames should be provided. Providing alternative text-only pages: When style sheets and/or frames are turned off it should be possible for the user to read and understand the page; alternatively, the user should be provided with an equivalent alternative text-only page.","[{""claim_id"": ""34-C1"", ""claim"": ""If frames are used, an alternative way of presenting relevant information without frames should be provided."", ""claim_text"": ""If frames are used, an alternative way of presenting relevant information without frames should be provided."", ""claim_kind"": ""OBSERVABLE_CORE"", ""claim_type"": ""OBSERVABLE"", ""importance"": ""CORE"", ""status"": ""MISSING"", ""source"": ""requirement_decomposition""}, {""claim_id"": ""34-C2"", ""claim"": ""Providing alternative text-only pages: When style sheets and/or frames are turned off it should be possible for the user to read and understand the page; alternatively, the user should be provided with an equivalent alternative text-only page."", ""claim_text"": ""Providing alternative text-only pages: When style sheets and/or frames are turned off it should be possible for the user to read and understand the page; alternatively, the user should be provided with an equivalent alternative text-only page."", ""claim_kind"": ""OBSERVABLE_CORE"", ""claim_type"": ""OBSERVABLE"", ""importance"": ""CORE"", ""status"": ""MISSING"", ""source"": ""requirement_decomposition""}]",NFR,PARTIALLY_UI_VERIFIABLE,NONE,TEXT_OR_ELEMENT_PRESENCE,LOW,"An alternative text-only view may be visible, but behavior with stylesheets or frames turned off is not fully testable from screenshots."
0000 - cctns,35,"Consistent page layout: Pages should be designed using consistent layout schemes, supporting the user in finding similar information at the same position on different pages. Overall layout schemes apply to all pages and are preferable when all pages have a similar structure. Frequently, however, different pages have different purposes and types of content. In such cases, pages can usually be grouped in different categories, using one layout scheme for each category consistently.","[{""claim_id"": ""35-C1"", ""claim"": ""Consistent page layout: Pages should be designed using consistent layout schemes, supporting the user in finding similar information at the same position on different pages."", ""claim_text"": ""Consistent page layout: Pages should be designed using consistent layout schemes, supporting the user in finding similar information at the same position on different pages."", ""claim_kind"": ""OBSERVABLE_CORE"", ""claim_type"": ""OBSERVABLE"", ""importance"": ""CORE"", ""status"": ""MISSING"", ""source"": ""requirement_decomposition""}, {""claim_id"": ""35-C2"", ""claim"": ""Overall layout schemes apply to all pages and are preferable when all pages have a similar structure."", ""claim_text"": ""Overall layout schemes apply to all pages and are preferable when all pages have a similar structure."", ""claim_kind"": ""OBSERVABLE_CORE"", ""claim_type"": ""OBSERVABLE"", ""importance"": ""CORE"", ""status"": ""MISSING"", ""source"": ""requirement_decomposition""}, {""claim_id"": ""35-C3"", ""claim"": ""Frequently, however, different pages have different purposes and types of content."", ""claim_text"": ""Frequently, however, different pages have different purposes and types of content."", ""claim_kind"": ""OBSERVABLE_CORE"", ""claim_type"": ""OBSERVABLE"", ""importance"": ""CORE"", ""status"": ""MISSING"", ""source"": ""requirement_decomposition""}, {""claim_id"": ""35-C4"", ""claim"": ""In such cases, pages can usually be grouped in different c